        en: "The centre of Tabarka, built at the beginning of the French protectorate, has kept its old character. Have a drink at the Café Andalous, a traditional café in the heart of town, then walk along the marina where fishing boats sit beside yachts, and close by jewellery shops offer treasures of coral. Craftsmen also make pieces from the cork gathered in the region and from carved wood. Choose a high point in the town to enjoy the astonishing view over the bay, then linger at the tall rock needles carved by the sea, which glow at sunset in a magnificent display. Inland the mountain appears wrapped in a thick forest coat, and here stands the village of Aïn Draham with its red-tiled roofs.",
